Specification Prime Factors

DataType PrimeFactorization
Description A sequence of prime numbers whose product equals the original number.
Examples: ValidValues
| Value       | IsValid | Notes                                         |
| 2           | True    |                                               |
| 2,2         | True    |                                               |
| 2,2,3       | True    |                                               |
| 2,2,2,3,3,5 | True    |                                               |
| 1           | False   | 1 is not a prime number.                      |
| 4           | False   | 4 is not prime and must be factored into 2,2. |
| 2,4         | False   | Every factor must be prime.                   |
| 2,3,5       | False   | Not every list of primes is a valid result.   |
|             | False   | Factorization must not be empty.              |

Attributes FactorizationCases
| Name   | DataType           |
| Number | Integer            |
| Result | PrimeFactorization |

Calculation One Has No Prime Factors
Description One produces an empty factorization.
Examples: FactorizationCases
| Number | Result |
| 1      |        |

Calculation Prime Numbers Factor To Themselves
Description A prime number factors to itself.
Examples: FactorizationCases
| Number | Result |
| 2      | 2      |
| 3      | 3      |
| 5      | 5      |
| 7      | 7      |
| 13     | 13     |

Calculation Powers Of A Prime
Description Repeated prime factors are included once for each occurrence.
Examples: FactorizationCases
| Number | Result |
| 4      | 2,2    |
| 8      | 2,2,2  |
| 9      | 3,3    |
| 27     | 3,3,3  |

Calculation Composite Numbers
Description Composite numbers are represented by their prime factors.
Examples: FactorizationCases
| Number | Result |
| 6      | 2,3    |
| 10     | 2,5    |
| 12     | 2,2,3  |
| 15     | 3,5    |
| 21     | 3,7    |

Calculation Complex Factorizations
Description Prime factors are returned in ascending order.
Examples: FactorizationCases
| Number | Result              |
| 60     | 2,2,3,5             |
| 180    | 2,2,3,3,5           |
| 360    | 2,2,2,3,3,5         |
| 1024   | 2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2 |

Calculation Large Prime Number
Description Large prime numbers factor to themselves.
Examples: FactorizationCases
| Number | Result |
| 97     | 97     |
| 997    | 997    |